be parsed) to tell you what happened. To turn them off for a whole session,
set the option \code{taxastand.verbosity}:

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{options(taxastand.verbosity = "quiet")
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

The default is \code{"inform"}. Errors and warnings about problems with your
input (for example, a \code{taxon} that was not found) are always given. To
silence a single call, use \code{\link[=suppressMessages]{suppressMessages()}} or
\code{\link[=suppressWarnings]{suppressWarnings()}}, or \code{withr::with_options()}.
}

